# Runing clojure unit tests

- You can run the clojure unit tests with the make rule defined in [Makefile](mdc:math/Makefile) , but you need to be in the `math` directory:    
```
make test-clj
```
with optional argument `T` to specifi which namespace to test, e.g.
```
make test-clj T="instrument"
make test-clj T="pca"
```
as described in the test runner [test_runner.clj](mdc:math/test/test_runner.clj) 

# Clojure setup

Clojure runs in the docker container defined in [docker-compose.dev.yml](mdc:docker-compose.dev.yml) and [Dockerfile](mdc:math/Dockerfile) .
In it, we do not use `lein`, we use `clojure`.
[Makefile](mdc:Makefile) and [Makefile](mdc:math/Makefile) have useful rules to invoke commands related to these containers, in particular to run clojure code.